  "result": "The two decisions sit in these places:\n\n- **At sign-in:** `src/server/services/session-service.ts` sets `SESSION_TTL_DAYS = 30`. `createSessionToken` uses it to compute `expiresAt`, and the login action then sets the cookie's expiry from that value.\n- **On a later request:** `src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts` has `findSessionByTokenHash`, which returns `null` once the stored `expiresAt` is at or before the current time. `src/lib/session.ts` has `getSessionPrincipal`, which runs the same check again and returns `null` if the time has passed. That `null` is what sends the user back to sign-in.\n\nA session issued 30 days ago is right at that boundary, which matches a user who signed in a month ago being bounced.\n\n`src/lib/session.ts` also builds the cookie's `expires` value in `setSessionCookie`, but that only carries the sign-in decision to the browser.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/session-service.ts, src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts, src/lib/session.ts",
